WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.030
In 2004, one video rental
chain had 9,094 stores.

2
00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.950
By 2010, it had filed for bankruptcy,

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.290
facing new ways to rent and stream films.

4
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.690
Behind every new idea that wins,

5
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.010
and every old firm that loses,

6
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.000
there is someone who
decided to start something.

7
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.650
So why would someone risk their
savings to start a business,

8
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.380
and who else gets a say once it exists?

9
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.810
In this mission, you'll
meet the entrepreneur,

10
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.560
and see how new ideas destroy
old firms and create new ones.

11
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.700
Then you'll map the groups
who care what a firm does,

12
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.510
from employees to suppliers
to the local community.

13
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.060
Your mission: find out why
people start businesses,

14
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.790
and who else they must listen to.
